Home » blockchain » ETH’s trading volume grew much faster than BTC’s in first half of 2021
Ether’s trading volume grew faster than Bitcoin’s in the first half of this year, according to a new report from leading American crypto exchange Coinbase.
Taking data from 20 exchanges across the globe, the report revealed that the trading volume for Bitcoin reached $2.1 trillion for the period, up 489% from $356 billion over the first half of last year.
The second-most valuable crypto asset appreciated 895% over the 12-month period and 210% over the six-month period ending June 30. Coinbase attributed a number of factors to this including increased usage in decentralized finance, investor optimism in the network’s transition to proof-of-stake, and the rise of layer-two scaling solutions for the network.
