Flow Dapper Lab’s (FLOW’s) peak tweet volume came late on July 10 (red circle in the chart) in action to an extremely effective week that the property had, more than doubling its cost from $9 to over $18.
These examples show that, while an attack of tweets alone is not constantly a precursor of an upcoming rally, identifying unusual Twitter activity early on can cause a successful trade. It can be specifically beneficial when integrated with other metrics and a robust understanding of the coin-specific context.
